Z||000014||sqoach||08-30-2001||11:33 AM||||Well, I figured just painting the spoiler and stuff couldn't be too hard. I'm pretty good with the cans  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>cadaver, thanks for the heads up. I think someone must have installed some stiffer springs when they put on this other spoiler, because it stays up just fine.<P>I may also need some gaskets. The ones that came with it are ok, but I'd like some nicer ones. How much are new wing stand gaskets? Or if anyone here has a nice set, that'll work  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000015||fierodave||08-30-2001||02:00 PM||||You won't need stiffer springs if the lid won't stay up.....the spring load can be adjusted  there are three holes with a pin through it that hold the tension,  Just move the rod one hole back to make more tension and it will be just fine.  I hooked up a long strap to my <BR>come-a-long   and then to my wall in the garage and winched them back,  remove the pins, insert in the middle hole and them slowly release the tension.   Make sure pin heads end up behind the spring rod and your done.  Takes about 15 minutes to do and you don't need to remove the lid or anything but the air cleaner tube  so you can see down there.  Just did two of them in the last three weeks!  it's a snap.<BR>FD<BR> ||||reg||1
Z||000016||cadaver||08-31-2001||12:31 AM||||So all this time pontiac made different springs and you dont need them? I have seen them where you cant adjust for a wing enough so then you would need them.||||reg||1
